  "kind": "quirk",
  "title": "FIND and SEARCH match an empty find_text at start_num, reject start_num past length+1, and floor start_num near integer boundaries",
  "statement": "In Excel 16.0.20527, FIND and SEARCH accept an empty find_text and return start_num (default 1), and return #VALUE! when start_num <= 0 or start_num > LEN(within_text) + 1 (or when the needle is not found). SEARCH supports ?, *, and ~ wildcards, while FIND matches literally with case sensitivity; both apply Excel's tolerant floor to fractional start_num values.",
  "status": "measured",
  "basis": "Measured in Excel 16.0.20527.20088 in f2_rows (rows 24-27) and matched across 2,863/2,863 FIND and 2,857/2,857 SEARCH full-bank witness rows (dc-ymjf.2.127).",
